{"n": 1657, "url": "https://www.creatio.com/page/bpmn", "title": "Business Process Modeling in BPMN Notation | Creatio", "verdict": "UNCERTAIN", "reason": null, "judgment": false, "evidence": "Creatio has been included in the Gartner Magic Quadrant for Intelligent Business Process Management Suites (2019)", "evidence_source": "page text", "record": "corpus/creatio/005_business-process-modeling-in-bpmn-notation.md", "needs_visual_check": false, "needs_human_ruling": true, "duplicate_of": null, "accessed": "2026-09-24", "surface": "creatio.com-landing", "question": "The page publishes eight full BPMN process diagrams (none of them containing an AI element) and five element-palette figures, one of which - 'System Actions in Creatio' - lists 'Predict data', the ML element that this same source records as putting a prediction model into a process (records 001, 003). Does a published palette of the designer's in-process element types count as an AI element bound into a process (page = corpus material, capture = the palette figure), or does 'AI element inside the process' require the element to be drawn inside a published process model (page = E2-no-ai-element)? Recorded UNCERTAIN rather than excluded: the element is an in-product process element and a wrong exclusion is unrecoverable.", "note": "Vendor marketing page (second surface of this source, reached from the assignment's entry points; the Academy's v10 guide tree is the other surface). Loaded in the real browser (chrome-devtools-mcp, own tab): no interstitial - the earlier Incapsula response was to the plain GET only. Eight figures are complete BPMN 2.0 process diagrams drawn in the Creatio process designer and were looked at directly (ledgers/_creatio/crm_bpmn_sheet.png, crm_sheet2.png); the page's own prose names the notation standard ('BPMN notation elements look the same in any program.'). Five figures are the designer's element palettes ('User Actions', 'System Actions in Creatio', 'Start events', 'Logical operators', 'Subprocesses'). No AI/LLM token occurs in the page text, any figure alt text or any figure file name except 'Intelligent' inside the Gartner award line quoted as the evidence, which names an analyst category, not a process element; the one AI-bound element name on the page is 'Predict data' inside the System Actions palette figure. Record 005 written, three captures."}
